        "base": "https://www.wananga.com/feed/rss2",
        "language": null,
        "type": "text/html",
        "value": "<div>\n  <h3>\n    <span>\n      <span>\n        \n            P\u016bkenga - Te Whare Aronui\n           \n      </span>\n    </span>\n    <span>\n      \n           - CLOSED\n          \n    </span>\n  </h3>\n  <h5>\n    <span>\n      \n           1.0 FTE Full time x 2\n          \n    </span>\n  </h5>\n  <h5>\n    <span>\n      \n           \u014ctaki Campus\n          \n    </span>\n  </h5>\n</div>\n<div>\n  <p>\n    <strong>\n      \n           P\u016bkenga \u2013 Te Whare Aronui\n          \n    </strong>\n    <span>\n      \n           \u00a0\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           \u00a0\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           \u014ctaki Campus\u00a0\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           1.0 FTE Full time x two (2) positions\u00a0\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           \u00a0\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           Te Whare Aronui, at Te W\u0101nanga o Raukawa based in \u014ctaki are seeking two full time p\u016bkenga to assist with teaching and learning activities within this very busy team.\u00a0 \u016akaip\u014dtanga will be your guiding kaupapa as you support students to reconnect back to their t\u016brangawaewae through Iwi and Hap\u016b studies and be able to draw on your own marae, hap\u016b and iwi experiences.\u00a0 \u00a0\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           \u00a0\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           As a successful applicant you will be a proficient teacher, confident communicator in te reo M\u0101ori and english and be committed to instilling ng\u0101 taonga tuku iho into the full range of students from rangatahi to kaum\u0101tua and tauiwi.\u00a0 Wh\u0101naungatanga is a must in this role as you develop key relationships with other p\u016bkenga, \u0101konga, internal support services, academic whare and Kura.\u00a0 You will be highly organised, passionate, and well supported to assist with the delivery of this component both face to face but mainly in the online space.\u00a0\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           \u00a0\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <span>\n        \n            Applications close:\u00a0\n           \n      </span>\n    </span>\n    <strong>\n      \n           Sunday 9 February\n          \n    </strong>\n    <span>\n      <span>\n        \n            \u00a0\n           \n      </span>\n    </span>\n    <span>\n      \n           (if not filled earlier)\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <br />\n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           For further information or to apply, please contact:\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           \u00a0\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           Dionne Seng, Kaihaut\u016b Te Whare Tiaki Rawa\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <span>\n        \n            E.\n           \n      </span>\n    </span>\n    <a href=\"mailto:Dionne.seng@twor-otaki.ac.nz\" target=\"_blank\">\n      \n           Dionne.seng@twor-otaki.ac.nz\n          \n    </a>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           P. 06 3649011 xtn 757\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <br />\n    </span>\n  </p>\n</div>"
      }
